requires a separate written commercial license. The restriction does not apply
to users of independent software created with assistance from Klerm.

3. File- and package-level notices control

Where a file, package, dependency, asset, or directory contains a more specific
license or copyright notice, that notice controls. Nothing in the Klerm
Community Source License restricts rights granted directly by an upstream
copyright holder.

4. No automatic relicensing of contributions

Contributors retain copyright unless they sign a separate assignment or
